"b": "Peru has rewritten its public procurement law to make sustainability one of its founding principles.",
"x": [
"Peru has rewritten its public procurement law to make sustainability one of its founding principles. Law 32069, the General Law on Public Procurement, was published in June 2024 and has applied since April 2025, replacing the 2016 State Contracting Law.",
"The law moves Peru away from buying at the lowest price towards buying for value. Among its guiding principles are value for money, under which public bodies must maximise the value obtained from each contract, and sustainability, which requires responsible practices in the purchase of goods, services and works. In practice:",
"- contracting strategies now include market engagement to promote economic, social and environmental sustainability, and sustainability factors can earn bidders additional points;",
"- a new supplier performance system measures how registered suppliers deliver, with incentives for the best rated;",
"- public procurement of innovation allows contracts that include research and development where no suitable solution yet exists on the market; and",
"- preferences reward micro and small enterprises and suppliers that deliver outside Lima and Callao.",
"A new specialised agency, the Public Procurement Supervisory Body (OECE), attached to the Ministry of Economy and Finance, supervises the system and provides technical support.",
"The reform is ambitious and young. Lawyers have warned that its 389-article regulation risks over-regulation, and implementation will depend on the capacity of thousands of procuring entities across a decentralised state.",
"Why it matters. Peru shows how an upper-middle-income country can embed sustainability, supplier performance and innovation in the core law that governs all public purchasing, rather than in a separate voluntary policy. It offers a model for the region and a test of whether legal principles translate into different buying decisions."
],
"src": "Law 32069 (Congress of Peru); Ministry of Economy and Finance; CMS; GCSI / Hogan Lovells Cadwalader / One Family Foundation, 'Legal & Policy Frameworks for Social Innovation' (July 2026)",
"url": "https://www.gob.pe/institucion/oece/colecciones/45029-ley-n-32069-ley-general-de-contrataciones-publicas-y-su-reglamento"
